{"id":"s22","label":"22. Walpurgis-Night’s Dream","blocks":[{"k":"h","text":"OBERON AND TITANIA’s GOLDEN WEDDING","level":3},{"k":"h","text":"INTERMEZZO","level":3},{"k":"s","text":"MANAGER"},{"k":"v","lines":["Sons of Mieding, rest to-day!","Needless your machinery:","Misty vale and mountain gray,","That is all the scenery."]},{"k":"s","text":"HERALD"},{"k":"v","lines":["That the wedding golden be,","Must fifty years be rounded:","But the Golden give to me,","When the strife’s compounded."]},{"k":"s","text":"OBERON"},{"k":"v","lines":["Spirits, if you’re here, be seen—","Show yourselves, delighted!","Fairy king and fairy queen,","They are newly plighted."]},{"k":"s","text":"PUCK"},{"k":"v","lines":["Cometh Puck, and, light of limb,","Whisks and whirls in measure:","Come a hundred after him,","To share with him the pleasure."]},{"k":"s","text":"ARIEL"},{"k":"v","lines":["Ariel’s song is heavenly-pure,","His tones are sweet and rare ones:","Though ugly faces he allure,","Yet he allures the fair ones."]},{"k":"s","text":"OBERON"},{"k":"v","lines":["Spouses, who would fain agree,","Learn how we were mated!","If your pairs would loving be,","First be separated!"]},{"k":"s","text":"TITANIA"},{"k":"v","lines":["If her whims the wife control,","And the man berate her,","Take him to the Northern Pole,","And her to the Equator!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ORCHESTRA. TUTTI"},{"k":"d","text":"Fortissimo."},{"k":"v","lines":["Snout of fly, mosquito-bill,","And kin of all conditions,","Frog in grass, and cricket-trill,—","These are the musicians!"]},{"k":"s","text":"SOLO"},{"k":"v","lines":["See the bagpipe on our track!","’Tis the soap-blown bubble:","Hear the schnecke-schnicke-schnack","Through his nostrils double!"]},{"k":"s","text":"SPIRIT, JUST GROWING INTO FORM"},{"k":"v","lines":["Spider’s foot and paunch of toad,","And little wings—we know ’em!","A little creature ’twill not be,","But yet, a little poem."]},{"k":"s","text":"A LITTLE COUPLE"},{"k":"v","lines":["Little step and lofty leap","Through honey-dew and fragrance:","You’ll never mount the airy steep","With all your tripping vagrance."]},{"k":"s","text":"INQUISITIVE TRAVELLER"},{"k":"v","lines":["Is’t but masquerading play?","See I with precision?","Oberon, the beauteous fay,","Meets, to-night, my vision!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ORTHODOX"},{"k":"v","lines":["Not a claw, no tail I see!","And yet, beyond a cavil,","Like “the Gods of Greece,” must he","Also be a devil."]},{"k":"s","text":"NORTHERN ARTIST"},{"k":"v","lines":["I only seize, with sketchy air,","Some outlines of the tourney;","Yet I betimes myself prepare","For my Italian journey."]},{"k":"s","text":"PURIST"},{"k":"v","lines":["My bad luck brings me here, alas!","How roars the orgy louder!","And of the witches in the mass,","But only two wear powder."]},{"k":"s","text":"YOUNG WITCH"},{"k":"v","lines":["Powder becomes, like petticoat,","A gray and wrinkled noddy;","So I sit naked on my goat,","And show a strapping body."]},{"k":"s","text":"MATRON"},{"k":"v","lines":["We’ve too much tact and policy","To rate with gibes a scolder;","Yet, young and tender though you be,","I hope to see you moulder."]},{"k":"s","text":"LEADER OF THE BAND"},{"k":"v","lines":["Fly-snout and mosquito-bill,","Don’t swarm so round the Naked!","Frog in grass and cricket-trill,","Observe the time, and make it!"]},{"k":"s","text":"WEATHERCOCK"},{"k":"d","text":"towards one side"},{"k":"v","lines":["Society to one’s desire!","Brides only, and the sweetest!","And bachelors of youth and fire.","And prospects the completest!"]},{"k":"s","text":"WEATHERCOCK"},{"k":"d","text":"towards the other side"},{"k":"v","lines":["And if the Earth don’t open now","To swallow up each ranter,","Why, then will I myself, I vow,","Jump into hell instanter!"]},{"k":"s","text":"XENIES"},{"k":"v","lines":["Us as little insects see!","With sharpest nippers flitting,","That our Papa Satan we","May honor as is fitting."]},{"k":"s","text":"HENNINGS"},{"k":"v","lines":["How, in crowds together massed,","They are jesting, shameless!","They will even say, at last,","That their hearts are blameless."]},{"k":"s","text":"MUSAGETES"},{"k":"v","lines":["Among this witches’ revelry","His way one gladly loses;","And, truly, it would easier be","Than to command the Muses."]},{"k":"s","text":"CI-DEVANT GENIUS OF THE AGE"},{"k":"v","lines":["The proper folks one’s talents laud:","Come on, and none shall pass us!","The Blocksberg has a summit broad,","Like Germany’s Parnassus."]},{"k":"s","text":"INQUISITIVE TRAVELLER"},{"k":"v","lines":["Say, who’s the stiff and pompous man?","He walks with haughty paces:","He snuffles all he snuffle can:","“He scents the Jesuits’ traces.”"]},{"k":"s","text":"CRANE"},{"k":"v","lines":["Both clear and muddy streams, for me","Are good to fish and sport in:","And thus the pious man you see","With even devils consorting."]},{"k":"s","text":"WORLDLING"},{"k":"v","lines":["Yes, for the pious, I suspect,","All instruments are fitting;","And on the Blocksberg they erect","Full many a place of meeting."]},{"k":"s","text":"DANCER"},{"k":"v","lines":["A newer chorus now succeeds!","I hear the distant drumming.","“Don’t be disturbed! ’tis, in the reeds,","The bittern’s changeless booming.”"]},{"k":"s","text":"DANCING-MASTER"},{"k":"v","lines":["How each his legs in nimble trip","Lifts up, and makes a clearance!","The crooked jump, the heavy skip,","Nor care for the appearance."]},{"k":"s","text":"GOOD FELLOW"},{"k":"v","lines":["The rabble by such hate are held,","To maim and slay delights them:","As Orpheus’ lyre the brutes compelled,","The bagpipe here unites them."]},{"k":"s","text":"DOGMATIST"},{"k":"v","lines":["I’ll not be led by any lure","Of doubts or critic-cavils:","The Devil must be something, sure,—","Or how should there be devils?"]},{"k":"s","text":"IDEALIST"},{"k":"v","lines":["This once, the fancy wrought in me","Is really too despotic:","Forsooth, if I am all I see,","I must be idiotic!"]},{"k":"s","text":"REALIST"},{"k":"v","lines":["This racking fuss on every hand,","It gives me great vexation;","And, for the first time, here I stand","On insecure foundation."]},{"k":"s","text":"SUPERNATURALIST"},{"k":"v","lines":["With much delight I see the play,","And grant to these their merits,","Since from the devils I also may","Infer the better spirits."]},{"k":"s","text":"SCEPTIC"},{"k":"v","lines":["The flame they follow, on and on,","And think they’re near the treasure:","But Devil rhymes with Doubt alone,","So I am here with pleasure."]},{"k":"s","text":"LEADER OF THE BAND"},{"k":"v","lines":["Frog in green, and cricket-trill,","Such dilettants!—perdition!","Fly-snout and mosquito-bill,—","Each one’s a fine musician!"]},{"k":"s","text":"THE ADROIT"},{"k":"v","lines":["Sanssouci, we call the clan","Of merry creatures so, then;","Go a-foot no more we can,","And on our heads we go, then."]},{"k":"s","text":"THE AWKWARD"},{"k":"v","lines":["Once many a bit we sponged; but now,","God help us! that is done with:","Our shoes are all danced out, we trow,","We’ve but naked soles to run with."]},{"k":"s","text":"WILL-O’-THE-WISPS"},{"k":"v","lines":["From the marshes we appear,","Where we originated;","Yet in the ranks, at once, we’re here","As glittering gallants rated."]},{"k":"s","text":"SHOOTING-STAR"},{"k":"v","lines":["Darting hither from the sky,","In star and fire light shooting,","Cross-wise now in grass I lie:","Who’ll help me to my footing?"]},{"k":"s","text":"THE HEAVY FELLOWS"},{"k":"v","lines":["Room! and round about us, room!","Trodden are the grasses:","Spirits also, spirits come,","And they are bulky masses."]},{"k":"s","text":"PUCK"},{"k":"v","lines":["Enter not so stall-fed quite,","Like elephant-calves about one!","And the heaviest weight to-night","Be Puck, himself, the stout one!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ARIEL"},{"k":"v","lines":["If loving Nature at your back,","Or Mind, the wings uncloses,","Follow up my airy track","To the mount of roses!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ORCHESTRA"},{"k":"d","text":"pianissimo"},{"k":"v","lines":["Cloud and trailing mist o’erhead","Are now illuminated:","Air in leaves, and wind in reed,","And all is dissipated."]}]}